HST Office: sw layout test TestTdf150606 substitutes the document font its style gallery preview draws.

The style gallery of the HST ribbon draws each style's name in the style's own font, as the leading word processor
does (hst-style-gallery.patch, ribbon gallery patches). Upstream Writer has no such gallery in its default user
interface. After TestTdf150606 deletes its table, the gallery draws a style of tdf150606-1-min.odt that uses Gentium
Basic, which neither upstream nor HST bundles. On a user's system the font is substituted; in a CppunitTest the
test-only guard SAL_NON_APPLICATION_FONT_USE=abort aborts the whole CppunitTest_sw_layoutwriter run there, and hides
every later test of the suite. The test now maps Gentium Basic to the bundled Liberation Serif for its duration. The
document's text does not use the font (its layout would hit the same guard), so the layout it checks is unchanged.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: make CppunitTest_sw_layoutwriter.
---
--- a/sw/qa/extras/layout/layout.cxx
+++ b/sw/qa/extras/layout/layout.cxx
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@
 #include <osl/process.h>
 #include <comphelper/scopeguard.hxx>
 #include <comphelper/propertysequence.hxx>
+#include <vcl/outdev.hxx>
+#include <vcl/rendercontext/AddFontSubstituteFlags.hxx>
 #include <vcl/scheduler.hxx>
 #include <svx/svddef.hxx>
 
@@ -1371,6 +1373,16 @@ CPPUNIT_TEST_FIXTURE(SwLayoutWriter, testRedlineFlysInHeader)
 #if !defined(MACOSX)
 CPPUNIT_TEST_FIXTURE(SwLayoutWriter, TestTdf150606)
 {
+    // HST Office: the style gallery of the ribbon draws each style's name in the style's own font,
+    // as the leading word processor does (hst-style-gallery.patch). Once the table is deleted it
+    // draws a style of this document that uses Gentium Basic, which no build bundles: a user's
+    // system substitutes the font, but the test-only SAL_NON_APPLICATION_FONT_USE=abort guard ends
+    // the run. The text of the document does not use the font (its layout would hit the same
+    // guard), so the substitution leaves the layout this test checks unchanged.
+    OutputDevice::AddFontSubstitute(u"Gentium Basic"_ustr, u"Liberation Serif"_ustr,
+                                    AddFontSubstituteFlags::ALWAYS);
+    comphelper::ScopeGuard aRemoveSubstitute([] { OutputDevice::RemoveFontsSubstitute(); });
+
     createSwDoc("tdf150606-1-min.odt");
 
     SwWrtShell* pWrtShell = getSwDocShell()->GetWrtShell();
